<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-BB004-2>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-BB004-2" ;
  triage:title "PR #1484 hand-edits a synced sc-publish kit file in violation of ADR-050" ;
  triage:description "quality-mgr, BB-READY-004-QA1-1789287640 (PR #1484 @ 052773738, report 01M2CYJT9NJT20JAJD41R548ES). .claude/skills/prerelease/scripts/prerelease.py is a synced sc-publish kit file: release/sc-publish-pin.toml:14-16 marks the prerelease kit as vendored from sc-publish PR #90 @ cd6c52d4. ADR-050 (docs/adr/ADR-050-shared-publish-kit-ownership.md) forbids a local edit to a synced shared file -- 'ATM never locally edits a synced shared file. A shared defect is fixed upstream first and then adopted through an unchanged installer run.' Fenix independently verified sc-publish main (8d302bb8a, the #90 merge commit) is byte-identical to the vendored copy, confirming the wait_for_archive polling defect (BB-READY-004) genuinely exists upstream, not just locally." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-bb" ;
  triage:triageMode "fix_verification" ;
  triage:category "governance" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:source "quality-mgr, BB-READY-004-QA1-1789287640, verdict FAIL" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope ".claude/skills/prerelease/scripts/prerelease.py (ADR-050 shared-kit ownership)" ;
  triage:status "fixed" ;
  triage:dispatchReady false ;
  triage:triagedAt "2026-09-13T08:43:30Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:deferredNote "Lead ruling (2026-09-13, team-lead/fenix, ADR-050 -- no exception): upstream first, per ADR-050's explicit text. fenix is opening the wait_for_archive fix (plus kit tests covering the ATM-QA-BB004-1 clamp branch) as a sc-publish PR directly; once its CI is green and it merges, a new atm-core layer advances release/sc-publish-pin.toml to that merge commit and re-syncs the kit through an unchanged installer run, which also retires the stale 'vendored from unmerged #90' note (#90 itself merged 2026-09-09). PR #1484 is closed as superseded, not merged. BB-READY-004 stays open until the pin-advance layer passes fix-round QA; cipher's ATM-owned .just test additions from PR #1484 carry over into that layer. foundIn attributed to BB3 as bookkeeping reuse of a fully-closed sprint's branch slot (same convention as BB-READY-003/BB-READY-004), not a claim of origin -- no live atm-core fix branch exists yet pending the upstream merge. CLOSED (2026-09-13T09:13:00Z): quality-mgr BB-READY-004-QA2-1789291300 (PR #1487 @ 7c0711379, report 01M2D0MMCYNP5DS7MF9AYMSFE8) confirms fixed -- kit blobs byte-identical to sc-publish 390cc9ff1 via GitHub Contents API, pin note accurate (revision unchanged from the merge commit). No local hotfix; adopted through the unchanged installer run per ADR-050." ;
  triage:foundIn triage:BB3 ;
  triage:foundAt "2026-09-13T08:43:30Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-BB004-2/1> ;
  triage:hasOccurrence <urn:atm:triage:occurrence/ATM-QA-BB004-2/2> ;
  triage:hasResolution <urn:atm:triage:resolution/ATM-QA-BB004-2/1> ;
  triage:closedAt "2026-09-13T09:13:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
  triage:closedBy "quality-mgr" ;
  triage:triageRecordVersion "2" .

